Package: vroom
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Jonathan Baker <jon@vitund.ai>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: libc6, kmod, util-linux, e2fsprogs, systemd
Recommends: libcuda1 | libnvidia-compute
Description: use idle NVIDIA VRAM as swap or scratch disks
 vroom allocates video memory on an otherwise unused NVIDIA GPU through the
 driver's CUDA library and exposes it to the kernel as block devices (ublk
 or NBD), usable as high-priority swap, a mounted scratch filesystem in
 place of tmpfs, or a raw device.
 .
 Requires the proprietary NVIDIA driver (libcuda.so.1). Nothing is started
 on installation; devices are created with vroomctl.
